    "nowplaying": {
      "title": "SchemaNowPlaying",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "type"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "const": "nowplaying"
        },
        "style": {
          "enum": [
            "full",
            "bar",
            "card"
          ]
        },
        "idle": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 512
        },
        "notice": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 512
        },
        "weight": {
          "type": "number",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 100
        }
      },
      "description": "The OS music player view, bound to the media session: cover (the artwork, or a cover drawn from the title when there is none), title, artist, a format line, position bar, transport buttons, volume and, as a page variant, the queue. 'full' fills a page (variant 'queue' shows the queue beside the cover), 'bar' is a one-line mini player, 'card' fits a home card. 'idle' is shown while nothing plays; 'notice' is a line of text (a playback error) under the title. Buttons, the bar and the queue call the player directly; the plugin only provides the media."
    },
    "tv": {
      "title": "SchemaTv",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "type"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "const": "tv"
        },
        "channel": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 160
        },
        "tap": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*$",
          "maxLength": 64
        },
        "weight": {
          "type": "number",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 100
        },
        "fit": {
          "enum": [
            "contain",
            "cover"
          ]
        }
      },
      "description": "The OS television view: the cinema picture of 'video' (subtitles, buffering and error cards, brightness and volume by vertical drag) with a live-TV overlay in place of the transport bar. 'channel' is a state path to an object {number, name, group, line, lines, favorite, program:{title,start,end}, next:{title,start}} (times are epoch milliseconds, every field optional); the OS draws the channel banner, the programme now and next with its progress, and buttons for the previous / next channel, the channel list, the next line of the channel and the favourite mark. A button press, or a double tap on the left or right quarter of the picture, sends the 'tap' event with ('tap' value, action) where action is 'prev', 'next', 'list', 'line' or 'favorite'. The plugin only supplies the media and the channel."
    },
